// Recipes. Every recipe lists ingredients by "category" or by "item" key (an ingredient's
// key - its name in snake_case, e.g. "salt_pile" - or another recipe's id for synthesized
// materials). Elements of the chosen ingredients fill the effect lines; each tier is one of
//   {"at": N, "effect": "<effects.json key>"}
//       Strength follows vanilla alchemy: what you could brew right now (skill, perks,
//       Fortify Alchemy) from the strongest ingredient with that effect. A line's 1st, 2nd
//       and 3rd tier of an effect give 80%, 100% and 110% of that (+10% per further tier);
//       quality then scales the result. Override with "vanilla": 1.25, or give absolute
//       "magnitude" / "duration" to opt out (perks still apply).
//   {"at": N, "quality": +Q} {"at": N, "yield": +Y} {"at": N, "traitSlot": +1}
//   {"at": N, "element": "Fire", "amount": +A}   (materials: the product gains elements)
// For effect tiers only the highest reached tier per line applies.
// Discovery: "known" (from the start), "unlockSkill" (Alchemy level) and "unlocks" rules
// ("ideas"): synthesizing this recipe with an item / category / quality unlocks another.
